@prefix shacl: <https://vng.nl/shacl/> .
@prefix rdf:   <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix xsd:   <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .

shacl:ValidateHeight a shacl:Shape ;
    shacl:id "ValidateHeight" ;
    shacl:description """
This SHACL shape validates the height of geometries against the highest wall.
1. geom:IfcElementHeightShape targets every subject that has a geom:globalId (sh:targetSubjectsOf).
2. A SPARQL-based constraint (sh:sparql) reads geom:globalId and geom:bboxMaxZ (the top of the bounding box) of each target.
3. A sub-query calculates ?globalMaxZ, the maximum geom:bboxMaxZ over all elements whose rdf:type is ifc:IfcWall (the VALUES list can be extended with more IFC types).
4. A target is reported as a violation when ?bboxMaxZ - ?globalMaxZ > 1, which means its top is more than 1 unit above the highest wall.
5. The result message is "Height violation for GlobalId=[...]: bboxMaxZ=... minus globalMaxZ=... exceeds 1."
6. The severity is sh:Violation.
""" ;
    shacl:shapeUri "validate-height.ttl" .